There can be no doubt that as climate change leads to rising temperatures, there will be greater risk of heat stress or heat exhaustion and hyperthermia (4). If workers cannot stop for rest breaks to drink water, seek shade and rest now, then imagine what it will be like in the next two decades.
Seventy-seven years after the Philadelphia Declaration, we should question why we are not making enough progress. Labour is very much a commodity and one of the factors that sustains this is the pressure of the piece-rate wage system, quotas and targets.
