After paying out 100% of profits to "loyal shareholders", Naga World Hotel Casino terminates over 1,300 workers who worked through the pandemic - IUF Asia-Pacific
After paying out 100% of profits to “loyal shareholders”, Naga World Hotel Casino terminates over 1,300 workers who worked through the pandemic
After months of ignoring union calls to improve COVID-19 safety measures, Cambodia’s largest hotel leisure resort Naga World Hotel Casino announced the mass redundancy of over 1,300 workers for “business reasons”. The mass retrenchment includes over 600 union members and union leaders – including the union president, vice president and general secretary.
Although management claims that the job roles of 1,300 workers will no longer exist, over 700 casual workers in insecure jobs will be re-deployed to fill these roles. Similarly, management’s assertion that job cuts are due automation hide the fact that the company deliberately accelerated its plans to introduce new technologies, displacing workers in a pandemic.
More than 600 union members refused redundancy and are demanding the right to negotiate the terms and conditions of restructuring through their union. Having already terminated the union leadership, management refuses to negotiate.
The schedule of these meetings will be finalized in consultation with affiliates. The schedule and documentation will be provided in different languages in a members only section of this website.
"what we fear as women", we fight as a union!
Environmental deterioration is the consequence of the various damages caused (causes) to the environment, such as the melting of glaciers. These causes can be varied, as well as the consequences, so it is important to know what they are in order to avoid them or find solutions.
1 Why does environmental deterioration occur?
1.4 Population increase
1.6 Harmful gases
3.1 Solutions in society
There are different factors or aspects that influence the deterioration of the environment, such as the depletion of natural resources, the industry sector, forestry, habitat deterioration, species introduced into other habitats and pollution of any of its types. Pollution
It is possible to find different Types of pollution, since they are usually classified according to the affected environment. Among them the most common are those of the soil, atmospheric, hydric or water and acoustic, which are usually studied in school; but also light, visual, thermal, electromagnetic, radioactive, genetic and garbage (electronic and special) must be taken into account.
The point is when the contamination is located in a single point, such as a drain.
Afforestation For its part, it has become a highly artificial process, since plants have been modified to have a higher yield and reduce the probability of contracting some of the best-known diseases of trees or crops.
Habitat deterioration Due to the actions carried out by human beings, such as dams and coastal tourism, the natural conditions of the habitat have deteriorated, which represents a danger for the species of plants and animals that reside in it.
Each of the causes follows a process that ultimately affects the environment where we live, and which in turn is something we are aware of but ignore most of the time. Although the campaigns about environmental damage have had positive results, there is still a long way to go to raise awareness among the entire population.
It is true that for many reasons, we have to move by car. But it is also true that sometimes, although it is not so necessary, we also carry it.
The causes mentioned above are the ones that cause the most environmental damage; Of these we also explain their main consequences, although in a general way we can highlight the damages of greater magnitude and that need effective solutions, such as global warming, deforestation, the effects of soil exploitation, microclimates, negative effects on human health, among others that we will see below. 1.
Global warming is the product of rising temperatures that have been studied over the last century, which produces devastating effects on the environment. These occur to a greater or lesser impact depending on the geographical location and the deterioration produced in it; as well as the side effects of some of the causes.
Only global warming is a truly devastating consequence that must be addressed with the greatest possible urgency, since it has a large amount of damage that affects the world population, plant and animal species, and the entire ecosystem in general. 1.1.
The main damage produced is the soil erosion, because this would make it a non-productive area and brings with it many more consequences: endangered species, habitat modification and displacement of some populations.
b) Depletion of natural resources Natural resources are not unlimited, so their use should be controlled to avoid problems in the future, although the main idea would be to get the population to adapt to a more conscious thought.
Infrastructures are generally affected due to different causes. For example, floods generated by natural phenomena such as tsunamis, hurricanes and tornadoes.
Just read the published figures, since they reflect the number of deaths (more than 5 million a year) and diseases caused by water pollution; thus affecting the health of any species or living being.
Because he is the one who covers and protects the earth from the sun's rays, which are harmful. But it also yields worrying data, because all the pollution there is, is giving a clue that the ozone layer may be weakening each time.
Certainly at present there is a large number of contributions made by organizations, foundations, international treaties, among others for fight against the deterioration of the environment. However, due to the seriousness of the situation, it is necessary to provide many more solutions if we want effective results.
Political contributions Politicians and agencies in charge of caring for nature must create laws that regulate industrial activities or those of the inhabitants themselves (fines for polluting), for example.
Entrepreneurs and manufacturers, in addition to paying attention to laws and treaties regarding the control and maintenance of the environment, must also collaborate in finding solutions that allow them to reduce pollution.
If you like nature, do not miss these phrases to take care of the environment. You can share them on your social networks and thus make the people around you aware of how important it is for us to take care of the planet we live on.
