The sayings of life always accompany us and the best of all, is that they tell us much more than we can imagine. They are sayings that can make you reflect on a certain situation so that you better understand what is happening.
They are expressions that are transmitted from parents to children, from grandparents to grandchildren ... from generation to generation. It is an easy way to communicate with our loved ones by delving into important topics without explaining too much.
1.1 Knowledge does not take place
1.3 Sew and sing, everything is starting
1.7 It's better to prevent than to cure
1.9 You are the owner of your silence but the slave of your words
1.11 After the storm comes the calm
It is also possible that you have heard them but are not sure what they mean ... Therefore, let's show you some sayings but we will also explain their meaning so that you can use them in the right context when you need it.
If you propose something in life, be it personally or professionally ... learning is a duty and it never hurts to do so. Rejecting learning prevents growth and have enough tools to move forward in life.
We may even think that we will never be able to do it. Actually, we can achieve anything we set our minds to if we get enough skills to do it (within our personal capacities).
But when the first step is taken to begin, the most difficult is already overcome. When you start a project, a task or any other activity, we can move forward as long as we are willing to start.
No one is born knowing and mistakes are part of life. In this sense, it is normal that when you do something you are wrong, but by going back and starting again you will learn to be better in that skill the next time.
This saying is used a lot in families, when the son resembles the father or the daughter resembles the mother. It is normally used for both positive and negative connotations.
But this saying means that you cannot get carried away by appearances, because on many occasions the disappointment can be very great. You have to be cautious in life in all aspects and not get carried away only by what seems perfect.
This saying is very popular, and it basically focuses on the fact that it is better to be a cautious person than later to regret the consequences of having taken little thoughtful actions. Because, taking precautions is always the best way to avoid further suffering.
The rush is always bad advisers and companions, because they do not allow us to think clearly and in most cases they can make us make poor decisions that bring us bad consequences.
You are the owner of your silence but the slave of your words
If you harvest winds, you will have storms
After the storm comes the calm
