3 Show confidence in your words
When you write, you have no tools other than your way of expressing yourself, your knowledge and your confidence in what you write. Unlike oral communication, where you can use non-verbal language to convey feelings in listeners, When you write, you only have your words.
Thus, the reader does not lose the thread, nor does it disconnect as it progresses in the reading because everything is connected. His brain joins the words through the connections that you yourself are placing in the text.
