Why does environmental deterioration occur?
Is named contamination to the alteration of the environment by the introduction of elements that are not suitable or original, that is to say, it is basically the presence of any substance or object that does not belong to the habitat and causes a negative effect on it.
Diffuse refers to situations in which the presence of harmful substances are distributed in the environment, such as the acid produced in the rains by the combination of harmful compounds and the humidity of the air.
Agricultural industries They have changed considerably today, since previously the natural species of flora and fauna were maintained. However, today's agriculture is only concerned with using hybrid plants that according to them “benefit” the population; just like livestock.
The factories of goods, substances or anything are in constant production to satisfy a consumer society, which not only generates contamination with the processes carried out, but also offers the populations the agents or elements necessary to contribute to the deterioration of the half.
Environmental deterioration also occurs with the introduction of species in different habitats, since these do not originate from that place, they can break the life cycle of a species.
Also known as “felling of trees”, it refers in a general way to all that action carried out by man that produces forest destruction; which is generally the product of the felling of trees to build spaces with different objectives.
One third of the earth's population survives on less than thirty liters; while according to a study, a single tourist is capable of spending more than a thousand liters of water daily. Therefore, water is one of the most affected resources and it has truly alarming figures, as we mentioned earlier.
Human health and many species are affected by this phenomenon due to different causes, but the figures are truly alarming. For example, human quality of life can be significantly reduced by drinking contaminated water, breathing air infected with harmful substances, and diseases caused by pollution in general.
Biodiversity means the ecosystem set and the variety of living things that make up the earth. All of it is not recent, but the result of many years of evolution.
It is another of the most immediate consequences. There are more intense droughts and the snow will melt much sooner, so the sea level it is going to increase and can cause flooding at certain points.
The objective to be achieved is that both ordinary people who inhabit a city or town, as well as businessmen, manufacturers, politicians and other positions, are aware that the environment needs to be cared for correctly. Therefore, depending on the area, there will be several solutions that prevent or slow down the development of deterioration.
In social terms, all people must have intelligent energy consumption, keep the taps closed and not let the water run, use energy-saving light bulbs or LEDs, keep vehicles in good condition or choose electric ones, avoid using plastic as bags, recycle and classify waste, maintain the cleanliness of public and natural places, among others.
These are just examples of some effective and viable solutions, which despite being applied today, environmental degradation continues to increase. Therefore, it is necessary to help spread the information through the different communication media to attract people's attention and make this knowledge a learning process.
