2.2 Choose a working title
A script is a text that you write with a very different objective from that of other types of texts. The script aims to transform itself into a play, into a theatrical performance that other people will enjoy through all their senses.
You must organize your story by characters and by scenes, so that later it can be put into audiovisual practice. Nevertheless, to start writing a script it is not necessary to do it in this professional way, because frustration could ruin your idea.
Many renowned authors write their scripts by hand, rather than using the computer. This is because when writing by hand, it is easier to transform, add, remove and modify as your brain throws the ideas at you.
Don't waste time choosing the perfect title, because it can come as you write your script. Doing it before writing the story can make it completely transform, without becoming what you had in mind.
Having data on your characters makes it easier for you to create a good plot based on them.
