Because information is worth nothing if it is not expressed in a correct way, especially when it comes to such an important project. Therefore, in addition to researching and developing an idea, it is essential to know how to transform it into a hypothesis so that it acquires validity.
2.4 Debug your hypothesis
This must be based on existing knowledge and proven theories. Therefore, good research work is essential to be able to provide data with the hypothesis before presenting it.
It must be clear and precise. Since otherwise your deductions cannot be considered as reliable.
Limited and specific. This means that your hypothesis should be limited in scope, as these are the hypotheses most likely to be solved.
Before you start, organize very well all the information you have obtained during your investigations. It is essential that everything has a correct order, otherwise the results could be altered.
As you begin to write your hypothesis, you should ask a question that you want to get an answer to. This question must be clear, it must be focused on the topic of the hypothesis and it must be able to be investigated.
The answer to the initial question should be based on the data that you have previously obtained during your research. When writing your hypothesis, add clear and truthful information that you have obtained during your investigation.
Now is the time to formulate your hypothesis
For a hypothesis to be investigated, it is essential that it is well written. So you must use clear terms that can be easily understood and that are related to the chosen topic.
Reading your hypothesis should be easy, even taking into account that it is going to be read by a scientist, do not assume that it must be written with complex and far-fetched terms. The easier it is to read, the more likely an answer will be found.
Before starting to make your hypothesis, organize the information very well, classify it and ask the necessary questions to be able to transfer them correctly to the writing. In this way, you can write an outstanding project.
Emotional dependence does not only occur in relationships, it can also occur in friends, family, co-workers, etc. When you need constant support from other people Regardless of you first, we may even be talking about pathological emotional dependency.
1 What is the meaning of emotional dependence
Emotional dependence is a personality disorder that is known as an anxious personality disorder. The person who suffers from it feels weak and powerless in the face of life circumstances, they are submissive people, and on many occasions, unable to take care of themselves.
Some signs that can make it clear that you are an emotionally dependent person are the following:
You require the help of others in order to carry out your responsibilities.
You are able to maintain a submissive attitude in the face of degrading or mistreatment circumstances only out of fear of rejection or abandonment.
When you end a relationship with one person, you desperately seek the beginning of another, for example, in relationships.
Sometimes a person who is emotionally dependent can be more difficult to detect when they are capable of making decisions in their daily life and they function well as professionals, but they feel great anxiety or insecurity when someone disapproves or rejects them. They do not know how to find the balance between emotional intimacy and autonomy.
This will end in a totally unhappy life, with abuse, manipulation and a ultimately toxic relationship. This can occur in couples, families, friends, colleagues ... Usually codependency occurs when your own needs are neglected to meet the needs of the other.
You will be able to address the underlying causes and also work on your insecurity, anxiety, stress, or irrational fears. Work on your inner strength so that you realize that you are capable of leading a happy and fulfilling life.
Work your emotional intelligence
Little by little you will begin to feel better and realize that if you go first in your life, you will feel good about yourself and the rest of the world.
