Normally most devices don’t use 192.168.0.0 as an IP address because once it is used as an IP address for the particular network and if admin tries to assign 192.168.00 to any device on the network as a static IP address, the entire network will shut down until the device is detached.
That’s the reason why devices with IP address ending with zero are normally not used.
