What was education like in Mexico in 1940?
What did the Government of Mexico neglect in education in the 40s?
Education in ancient Mexico was compulsory and free. However, education was not given in the same way for all inhabitants: there were schools for upper class, middle class and lower class children.
The new socialist orientation of education proposed to expand educational opportunities for urban and rural workers. Between 1936 and 1940 boarding schools, dining rooms and scholarships were created, the creation of schools linked to production centers was promoted and technical education was encouraged.
