Educational guidance is a systematic process of assistance to people in the training process, whether in the personal or professional sphere, whose objective is to develop vocational behaviors that help them in their adult life.
The educational guidance aims to help the correct development of students by personalizing the teaching-learning process adapted to the characteristics of each individual and advising students and families.
The concept of orientation is linked to the verb to guide. This action refers to placing something in a certain position, to communicate to a person what they do not know and that they pretend to know, or to guide a subject to a place.
Educational guidance is a teaching modality that transcends the regular content of classes and goes beyond the classroom, to teach and guide young people in the correct way to use their personal resources.
In short, orientation takes on special importance because it is considered a process capable of motivating personal self-management, the management of life skills and the development of positive attitudes towards a world subjected to recurrent transformations and exposed to conflicts.
