Recently, Martin Fraguio, CEO of the Argentine Corn Industry Association (Maizar), said that Argentine corn ethanol producers are preparing to increase production by as much as 60%, depending on how much the government will increase the blending rate of ethanol in gasoline. In April this year, the Argentine government increased the blending rate of ethanol by 2% to 12%.
It may be difficult for Argentine sugar producers to continue to increase ethanol production, while corn growers will increase corn plantings for 2016/17, as President Markley canceled corn export tariffs and quotas after taking office. He said that the further increase in ethanol production can only come from corn.
