Chain and chain slings require careful storage and regular maintenance.
Store chain and chain slings on an “A” frame in a clean, dry place.
To protect both operators and materials, observe these precautions when using chain slings.
Before use, inspect chain and attachments following the inspection instructions.
Do not exceed working load limit as indicated on the chain or chain sling identification tag. Any of the following factors can reduce the strength of the chain or sling and cause failure:
Variation in the angle of the load to the sling. As the angle decreases, the working load of the sling will increase.
Do not drop load on chains.
Match the size and working load limit of attachments such as hooks and rings to the size and working load limit of the chain.
