This scenic city with population of over 3 million people is located on the shores of the Dnepr River.
Everyone will find there something especially interesting for himself.
In the historical center of Kiev you can feel the spirit of the past everywhere.
Theater lovers will find many theatres offering various theatrical programs.
The recently renovated Kiev Opera House presents very good opera as well as a broad repertoire of ballets.
A lot of various exhibitions are carried out in the city’s numerous museums and art galleries.
Various universities and science academies including famous Kiev-Mogilyanskaya Academy, which is one of the first scientific establishments in Eastern Europe, are located there.
Kiev’s major industries include: food processing (especially processing of beet sugar), metallurgy, manufacture of machinery, machine tools, rolling stock, chemicals, building materials, and textiles.
There are a lot of new office centers, banks, trade exhibition centers and other commercial enterprises appearing in the city nowadays.
For sure your stay in Kiev will become one of your most memorable experiences.
