It is a quiet, incredibly green city with a unique atmosphere, bright history and a plethora of interesting natural, historical and architectural sights.
Another legend claims that the city was named after its founder, Grand Crown Hetman Jan Tarnowski.
In the Middle Ages, Ternopil stood at the intersection of important trade routes, becoming an important center of commerce.
In the 19th century, the castle was turned into a Russian classicist palace, and its remaining defenses were annihilated.
At that time, it was often used to defend the city.
The lake is as old as the city itself: it was created at the same time as the castle.
Many distinct historic, architectural and cultural landmarks can also be found on Ternopil’s outskirts: almost every town and every village you will contains the ruins of some medieval castle, ancient church or monastery.
The first documentary record about the city dated in the XII century.
The city has its own emblem and the flag.
Institutions of local government are presented by local city council and the head of the city (the mayor).
Climate In general our city climate is temperate, continental with chilly winter and warm (sometimes sultry summer).
During al this time the average annual temperature increased approximately on 1,5 °C. The warmest year, according to long-term observation, was the year of 2010.
It was reduced up to 14 thousand people in comparison with the year of 1989 – and it is not so bad indicator, taking into account the demographic situation in Ukraine (for example, the population of Lvov reduced up to 57 thousand people for this period of time).
87% of the city population are Ukrainians; 44, 0% of hard-working population are involved into industrial sphere; 16, 0% — into service sphere; 6, 0% — into science, art and education.
Our city is a place, where important railway tracks and highways are intersected.
Kiev-Kharkov route is electrified and provides the way of fast and comfortable trains.
There are 12 higher educational establishments on the territory of our city.
In our city there are 52 general education establishments and 54 preschool institutions, among which: 14 new type institutions (city lycées and gymnasiums).
That is why on its territory there are so many enterprises, specializing in fuel, food, light and woodworking industries.
Our city gives 1/4 of industrial region production.
