It is a crime novel published in February 2017 and, like the first book, is set in Suances. The story takes place months after the previous plot and unfolds in the middle of an enigmatic murder.
After this event, a wave of murders is unleashed in the area, which turns on the alarms again. In view of the dreadful scenery, Lieutenant Redondo along with her colleagues from the Civil Guard decide to start the hunt for the murderer.
Valentina is looking forward to the end of the summer to go on vacation with Oliver. But everything turns upside down when receiving the call for a new case: the gardener of the Palace of the Master appeared dead.
At first, it was presumed that the man's death had been due to natural causes, but the investigation showed that someone had touched the corpse.
Although the lieutenant is skeptical about the paranormal, she, Oliver, and her team are caught up in inexplicable events..
It is an independent thriller in which Lieutenant Valentina Redondo and her colleagues from the police investigation force continue to be the protagonists. In November 2021, in Spain, the work received the distinction of best fiction book of the year by the booksellers of “El Corte Inglés”.
Until now, The series has three additional novels: A place to go (2017) Where we were invincible (2018) y What the tide hides (2021). Likewise, his collection is complemented by individual work: The forest of the four winds (2020).
