we are going to show you how to know if my wifi is stolen, as well as how to block them. In this way, those people who are accessing your WiFi network without permission will not be able to enter again.
Table of Contents 1 Signs that my WiFi is being stolen
4.2 Be careful who you share the key with
Signs that my WiFi is being stolen
You have noticed that something is different with your connection and it is possible that other people are entering your network without permission. The normal thing is that we have noticed that there are some changes in this connection, in its operation, which makes us think that someone has entered without permission.
The Internet connection slows down at very specific moments or times of the day (always at the same time, for example).
The normal thing is that this happens, that the connection suddenly works worse, without there being a clear reason for it (there is no fault or works in your area). So if this happens, it is normal to think that someone is using our WiFi without permission.
If we want to check who is connected to our WiFi network, the best and easiest way to do this is by accessing the router directly through the web address on the bottom of the device. Next to that address, we will find the username and password to access the router, which is different from the password for its WiFi signal.
We are only going to have to enter this in the browser on our device, to access that menu with router options. Here you can see that we have a series of options, some of them possibly too complex for many users, but that will allow us to see the devices that are connected to our network at that moment.
Therefore, below we leave you with some of these apps we can use to know this. To be able to see who is using our WiFi network and the way in which we can expel them from it in a simple way.
Networl Analyzer is one of the best applications in this field that we have available in the Play Store. This app will allow us to perform an analysis of our WiFi network.
This is an app that we can Download for free from the Play Store. The app has a free version with ads, as well as a paid version that gives us access to a series of additional functions.
If we have already detected those devices connected to our network without permission and we have also expelled them, it is time to take action. We must prevent others from being able to connect to this WiFi network without our permission.
Since there will be letters, numbers, varying between uppercase and lowercase, for example, as well as some symbol or character that is not usual. These types of keys are much more complicated to hack, so we will prevent others from being able to connect to our WiFi without our permission.
If you have people who come to visit or if you share the key with other people, it is important that you are going to be careful with those people to whom you give your WiFi key. You don't want anyone to have access that they shouldn't have, so it's good to limit the number of people who have access to your network.
Another method that can work to prevent others from stealing or entering our WiFi without permission is this, the use of the Mac connection. Every device with an Internet connection on the market has a Mac address or connection.
It's something that all users can configure on their devices. In this way, every time we want a device to connect to our Wi-Fi network, it is necessary to manually enterthe Mac on the router via its login page.
