If you have bought a silicone mobile phone case, especially transparent silicone ones, you will have noticed that with the passage of time and use, this case gets darker and darker, until it ends up becoming a yellowish cover.
But this problem it can be prevented, and there are solutions for it. Here is everything you need to get rid of this problem once and for all.
1 Are there anti-yellowing covers?
3 How to prevent this problem?
5 Maintenance of your cover
exist mobile phone cases that have special treatments or chemical compositions that help delay or prevent yellowing with time and use. Therefore, if you want to forget about these problems, you should take a look at some of the anti-yellowing cases that exist on the market for your mobile device.
There is a huge variety. But the polymer ones, especially the transparent ones, always tend to darken over time and turn a yellowish color.
How to prevent this problem?
In fact, given the cheap price they usually have, in many cases the best option is to directly discard the cover and buy a new one if you prefer. It is not mandatory, since that tone does not affect the properties of these protectors, but it can be something that affects aesthetics.
Before proceeding, remove the mobile phone case to prevent it from getting wet. And, before putting the cover back on once it's clean, make sure it's completely dry.
A method to clean the yellowish cover of your mobile is as simple as use soap and water.
Find a container where you can submerge the sleeve.
With the help of a toothbrush or a rough sponge, rub all the areas and corners of your cover.
It only remains to dry using a soft cloth. If you let it dry for a few hours so that it loses all moisture, the better.
This not only disinfects, it can also remove some embedded stains. To clean the cover:
With it rub the cover everywhere.
Finally, rinse the cover with water and dry very well.
Vinegar is always combined with baking soda in many home remedies. On this occasion it can be used alone, for its acidic properties that help clean surfaces and for its antimicrobial properties.
Put a little apple or normal grape vinegar (never balsamic or Modena vinegar, as they have sugar and leave residue), and a few drops of lemon juice too.
Use a cloth to blot up all the vinegar. If it smells too much of vinegar, you can rinse with water if you want.
You can finally put your cover back on.
Finally, it is another of the most powerful cleaners you have at home. You can use any kind of bleach, no matter the brand, nor whether it is scented or not.
Mix well and leave the cover for 1 hour to act.
Remember good maintenance of your case to prevent it from being a yellowed case. That is washing your hands before picking up your mobile, preventing dust and dirt from accumulating over time, and disinfecting surfaces, since a large number of bacteria usually appear on these frequently used objects.
